  "effect_semantics": {
    "friction": "Coulomb plus viscous torque opposes measured joint velocity; near zero speed the drive-torque sign is used without allowing friction to reverse the commanded direction.",
    "stiction": "A stateful enter/exit velocity hysteresis holds zero net torque below breakaway and releases only above breakaway torque or the exit-speed threshold.",
    "backlash": "A one-dimensional play operator transforms position targets and retains transmitted target across direction reversals until the half-width dead zone is crossed.",
    "compliance": "A bounded first-order torsional transmission state uses stiffness, damping, and maximum elastic deflection; it is a noncalibrated reduced-order gear/joint model.",
    "identification": "Each step exposes a deterministic sample and accumulator for future friction, reversal, stiction, backlash, and compliance identification without callbacks from the physics thread.",
    "disablement": "Each effect has an independent runtime switch; with every effect disabled the wrapped ServoModel result and position target are preserved exactly."
  },
